                            "event": "message.complete",
                            "seq": 41,
                            "text": "The Development Finance Observatory (DFO) holds 202,216 indicators across 95 datasets from 43 publishers, covering 246 countries. Aid data covers 172 donors and 235 recipients from 1960 to 2025.\n\nIts core datasets cover:\n\n* **Official Development Assistance and Aid:** Detailed aid activities from the OECD Creditor Reporting System (CRS) by donor, recipient, sector, channel, and financing type, as well as ONE Imputed Multilateral Sectors data.\n* **External Debt:** Stocks, flows, and debt service for low- and middle-income countries from the World Bank's International Debt Statistics (IDS).\n* **Macroeconomic Indicators:** GDP, output gaps, savings, investment, and projections from the IMF World Economic Outlook (WEO).\n* **Socio-economic, Health, and Development Data:** Series from the World Bank's World Development Indicators (WDI), the WHO Global Health Observatory, the UN SDG Indicators Database, and other regional and national sources via Data Commons.\n\nYou can ask for specific figures, comparisons across countries or donors, sector breakdowns, or trends over time."
